Ownership of the Pipelines for Tokenized U.S. Assets
The “pipelines” you’re referring to are the interbank and blockchain settlement systems that will move tokenized U.S. assets — such as tokenized Treasuries, deposits, and other real-world 
assets — in near real time.

1. For the Ondo/Kinexys/Mastercard/Ripple pilot (tokenized U.S. Treasuries)
In the May 2026 cross‑border settlement, the XRP Ledger handled the on‑chain asset movement, Mastercard’s Multi‑Token Network (MTN) routed payment instructions, and Kinexys by J.P. Morgan 
delivered the dollar leg via J.P. Morgan’s correspondent banking network 
genfinity.io
genfinity.io
.

Kinexys is owned and operated by J.P. Morgan.

Mastercard is a global payments company, so its MTN is owned by Mastercard.

The XRP Ledger is maintained by Ripple.
Thus, in this specific pilot, the “pipelines” are owned by Ripple, Mastercard, and J.P. Morgan.

2. For the Cari Network (tokenized bank deposits)
The Cari Network is a permissioned blockchain platform for tokenized FDIC‑eligible deposits, with Fireblocks providing the operational infrastructure and ZKsync Prividium handling the 
blockchain layer 
