.

Fireblocks is a private blockchain infrastructure company.

ZKsync Prividium is a Layer‑2 blockchain protocol.
The network is driven by Eugene Ludwig and supported by six design partner banks (Huntington, First Horizon, M&T Bank, KeyBank, Old National, SouthState), but the underlying technology is 
owned by Fireblocks and ZKsync.

3. For the shared bank deposit token network (JPMorgan, Bank of America, Citi, Wells Fargo)
This is a joint initiative by the four major U.S. banks, operated by The Clearing House — the payments company they already own together 
